-5e18-9063-2683b6b0394d" :question/math-academy-id "q-161593" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/80bde6a20ceed7c052a87eda6f05c542f6046de7014f6402f5f453b6610f8d42.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/05b25521109f373e2a7718523ce6289b27b37bd185d4fc60f0d052c232f4f8a4.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the line $y=-1+x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y=-1+x\\,}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161593/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e534c006-a5b4-5f76-bbd6-451496358d3a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161593"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-158313"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/c2452160f8af4651bdc78756b7c0df8402de185ba7a7bedbc1c1a676b342af97.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/eea68ab4e4b440609fcc4f6c2d40c4dc9fc394fc45f1047ec9c658729322749a.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the parabola ${y}^{2}=4x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{y}^{2}=4x\\,}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-161598/selection/6449b340535d115429d6fcd25695568612ab6404ada6400aa53665f8c6bd3bff" :answer/id #uuid "a27ee62b-a7a9-5a02-afe8-c855edc4adbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}>36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161598/selection/da8e32cfefe93dff8de615613cd0864f4ebef28d7a7b92ee9f1f847c01d99d0e" :answer/id #uuid "0da20030-e113-5726-9bb4-36b205b8e036" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\ge 36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161598/selection/ac497a6a8f553f522cd8e3792892e656d7c49bf13b49ce28627bfab3bf955830" :answer/id #uuid "d24298c2-bc97-5830-a89b-d8d2b4de4308" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\le 36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161598/selection/a58e47cea51d9c5fb3b62fcc8faa968ae2d71489e903cb80635ba0c25439d3d2" :answer/id #uuid "aae007dc-f538-5498-80ec-fe74d572d1e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161598/selection/175792374a7ed887d0439c346d84978a274ce6f86b61e273a2ad970acfb7b79f" :answer/id #uuid "244a0dd3-1c2f-5bd6-9762-8c20ce0cf886" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161598/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "02d7cd99-5e48-55ff-b82d-4b505d9773bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161598/selection/a58e47cea51d9c5fb3b62fcc8faa968ae2d71489e903cb80635ba0c25439d3d2" :answer-field/choices ["q-161598/selection/6449b340535d115429d6fcd25695568612ab6404ada6400aa53665f8c6bd3bff" "q-161598/selection/da8e32cfefe93dff8de615613cd0864f4ebef28d7a7b92ee9f1f847c01d99d0e" "q-161598/selection/ac497a6a8f553f522cd8e3792892e656d7c49bf13b49ce28627bfab3bf955830" "q-161598/selection/a58e47cea51d9c5fb3b62fcc8faa968ae2d71489e903cb80635ba0c25439d3d2" "q-161598/selection/175792374a7ed887d0439c346d84978a274ce6f86b61e273a2ad970acfb7b79f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161598" :question/id #uuid "bcfdd46f-14ab-5535-a276-fcd0db509adc" :question/math-academy-id "q-161598" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/112ab676fa5a97db198a872c33579900deab76e0c3c9c92016e165a67482bbcd.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/44f3a2a8e535c7248dac49d126da9bf17fce94c357f15c93a3eaad665e73b47a.png)\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the ellipse ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36.$  \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36\\,}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161598/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e534c006-a5b4-5f76-bbd6-451496358d3a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161598"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161590/selection/a33c2e2b73e350d80ac941953897c291ad8f1f5139aa1e16ab411ecc351d543c" :answer/id #uuid "18a83002-9b42-5830-9e58-50acf6cd7024" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\ge 16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161590/selection/e8fb4a0e77a874472f92fc6f37f14e6e9b536f1a055635144011834b223b2343" :answer/id #uuid "55ad9afd-b849-5211-811f-e604a7159a59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}>16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161590/selection/78442837b329fdb16f619bac38e499ef310b875172ebd7b0b1ce7b5cca0c6e94" :answer/id #uuid "7cb2982c-07d6-5470-b21e-fbea1fb4efc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161590/selection/7a05c7112fb14d0e72b15540a4600dec78859dc3be1f6a84283830006781d8e1" :answer/id #uuid "7772eccd-6e38-5abf-a54e-8586c460ef18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161590/selection/fb82f3da47af3de708b4b0a8d36589b917a111ea75c76a1bd0687e5841cfccbf" :answer/id #uuid "f60dd168-6989-578f-ac25-6627ee5af362" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\le 16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161590/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "959c2d3c-c8fc-5ee1-aca0-44e95cc4a1d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161590/selection/78442837b329fdb16f619bac38e499ef310b875172ebd7b0b1ce7b5cca0c6e94" :answer-field/choices ["q-161590/selection/a33c2e2b73e350d80ac941953897c291ad8f1f5139aa1e16ab411ecc351d543c" "q-161590/selection/e8fb4a0e77a874472f92fc6f37f14e6e9b536f1a055635144011834b223b2343" "q-161590/selection/78442837b329fdb16f619bac38e499ef310b875172ebd7b0b1ce7b5cca0c6e94" "q-161590/selection/7a05c7112fb14d0e72b15540a4600dec78859dc3be1f6a84283830006781d8e1" "q-161590/selection/fb82f3da47af3de708b4b0a8d36589b917a111ea75c76a1bd0687e5841cfccbf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161590" :question/id #uuid "27e84be7-f3dd-5b1a-a260-43fabfe78370" :question/math-academy-id "q-161590" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\le 16}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/b1074330fc650cf6af682f173f50943d779819afa59bf5be19edb88def1ef03a.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the ellipse ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=16.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=16\\,}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161590/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e534c006-a5b4-5f76-bbd6-451496358d3a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161590"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161599/selection/c9949df5a9b8d680d46941bb0c31424d4ca1f6dc6260e499c4f0f4e9cbd528ce" :answer/id #uuid "0f4ee260-3bc9-5400-bf56-47d9322bb48f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2y\\ge {x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161599/selection/9d8782bb5995ac201948c9e459f64369a3d2216011ffd48c1687378d6d8d1018" :answer/id #uuid "cda9f910-7acf-595d-a614-b3cf5d1ee5e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2y\\le {x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161599/selection/338eb644270cdf200cc5fc75ee7409d81b339f535fceabdfbe7be8d19209f3f5" :answer/id #uuid "ce412e86-0c45-5e9f-9ab5-f337efcf6dae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2y<{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161599/selection/6fcc5d4d70331068d7281b7553ca5f16f880c0e0eb302506e7fe538841275113" :answer/id #uuid "7f764a67-5694-5182-896d-ef7b4c967bbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2y>{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161599/selection/205e9d433afe9fbfaf917e7acc25704f67e48703624f88a0046639a8b7436ee6" :answer/id #uuid "0e067a2d-a6f5-52ff-b110-b65c2fa82a74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2y={x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161599/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "af304b58-5892-5cc4-8da6-3654443376de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161599/selection/205e9d433afe9fbfaf917e7acc25704f67e48703624f88a0046639a8b7436ee6" :answer-field/choices ["q-161599/selection/c9949df5a9b8d680d46941bb0c31424d4ca1f6dc6260e499c4f0f4e9cbd528ce" "q-161599/selection/9d8782bb5995ac201948c9e459f64369a3d2216011ffd48c1687378d6d8d1018" "q-161599/selection/338eb644270cdf200cc5fc75ee7409d81b339f535fceabdfbe7be8d19209f3f5" "q-161599/selection/6fcc5d4d70331068d7281b7553ca5f16f880c0e0eb302506e7fe538841275113" "q-161599/selection/205e9d433afe9fbfaf917e7acc25704f67e48703624f88a0046639a8b7436ee6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161599" :question/id #uuid "626b0475-a4cb-5242-a0c8-33a38a54ece8" :question/math-academy-id "q-161599" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2y\\ge {x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/0fc95ee69ce7121c0cf8ae68029b135d9667f50275227d141f1d979f85408859.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the  parabola $-2y={x}^{2}.$ \n\nTherefore,  \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2y={x}^{2}\\,}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161599/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e534c006-a5b4-5f76-bbd6-451496358d3a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161599"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-158314"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/b95c538613ee8672e0f1cac970b7af230ec40bf3075e609b1e03f7cad4382fb1.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<1,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/19e8e52881066864cba562ed2a8cdc2944b9dae416c7124fdee207cdad1d8bdf.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/907e996fb7aea36e0c924feb0f5d9dc6804c768be775953d277e84b0145ef5a0.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<1,\\,-1<y<0}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-161700/selection/31cfd0e527580e825de0bcf5dbb39ba15ce1b608de9e0951e24bd24f3673e77e" :answer/id #uuid "b3a05b0d-6604-5fc1-a06b-0bedf50272a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161700/selection/6006a040e1952e10335e6731b0c0e3a6bacc3409120ac17104bbf8fb4738ca45" :answer/id #uuid "8c748f1f-b4fe-5756-935d-5080dd2e4af2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161700/selection/0533bab46e2c49bbb1c6584639476ca0ce6762f48b2e28897a0f4462b81d7044" :answer/id #uuid "76b2cfe7-f5e5-5d21-8db4-c909d92e2a56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161700/selection/243bfa63163e4d973f55cfaf9f7458ecfd6773de50c79b90dd3027d0badbdb85" :answer/id #uuid "61261487-ebbc-5927-9fd8-3eb279c19248" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161700/selection/755c4d99df0a762d9536abb7f5c17c9e67c7f1c50fabcc8c384332c61d41819e" :answer/id #uuid "64710a2c-035f-51cf-9b70-0f5eded45816" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161700/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4e543fc1-f762-5bf7-8837-d7f1ae4f6c01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161700/selection/31cfd0e527580e825de0bcf5dbb39ba15ce1b608de9e0951e24bd24f3673e77e" :answer-field/choices ["q-161700/selection/31cfd0e527580e825de0bcf5dbb39ba15ce1b608de9e0951e24bd24f3673e77e" "q-161700/selection/6006a040e1952e10335e6731b0c0e3a6bacc3409120ac17104bbf8fb4738ca45" "q-161700/selection/0533bab46e2c49bbb1c6584639476ca0ce6762f48b2e28897a0f4462b81d7044" "q-161700/selection/243bfa63163e4d973f55cfaf9f7458ecfd6773de50c79b90dd3027d0badbdb85" "q-161700/selection/755c4d99df0a762d9536abb7f5c17c9e67c7f1c50fabcc8c384332c61d41819e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161700" :question/id #uuid "d21a66c2-1c83-597c-83d2-92810c6d2822" :question/math-academy-id "q-161700" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4,\\,0\\le x\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,,\\,0<x<1}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/d60700d57ddc72bb410b3136f546705676f83d23d9071ffe972c5163d11af549.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/75e0132cd3854f18e9ab409b7fd13af3898f78b5174647bf2b33b8438b9228cb.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<x<1}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161700/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f89386f9-8a2b-56eb-8521-7c1ddafcfd96"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161700"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71889/selection/4318611d6ddd6f506f8bcfc9cbe544c6ad54581c8bbf997752249ed11a19d3a0" :answer/id #uuid "95fd32f6-8baf-53be-9b17-65a9692681fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0\\le y\\le -x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71889/selection/55f7cd47fab49b33270b46a8e736a91ab9afadf4661b14e12e068edcde03a809" :answer/id #uuid "1c19ec69-57c6-5cef-822e-84038e4a1ed1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0<y\\le -x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71889/selection/000371690df376546f2f0f2933898a2cb6acba300dfb244e3786c6add6bf9ef1" :answer/id #uuid "981e1171-6971-5221-bea1-76d28fe0de8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-x<y<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71889/selection/e5d8bfe797efe9ebacd3364078c77637e0007d859c26ff4387e0366f530b6eb9" :answer/id #uuid "0790faa2-dbae-5f58-98b1-81e9bdbf30d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-x\\le y<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71889/selection/8b3f1227b3fe52b757ceb65a0ef5bc9f71fc8d3e317a41a3b5ecbc911c184428" :answer/id #uuid "5e9fbe3e-479e-50e9-97a2-58ef802961cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer