id #uuid "e3430876-1457-5775-9fe8-70276e1b4953" :question/math-academy-id "q-105176" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2\\le x<0,\\,0<y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,,\\,0<y<1\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/4f65a735e53130f633635fdfc8cd6de6c4fa39ed1fb7913ba9679bb07e73a6a0.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/c76cea9b33420bf6c2e03d8eecb105003ce8b4e619063cbf2b7fccd5bc596cb2.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<1\\,}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105176/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f89386f9-8a2b-56eb-8521-7c1ddafcfd96"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105176"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161625/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "b06acb3c-1b5f-5e4b-acd5-3d88191085f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161625/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "4982bc7f-6393-550c-8019-d27e45da89c3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II